# Force LF line endings everywhere.
#
# This repo is edited on Windows but its scripts run in WSL/Linux. A shell script
# checked out with CRLF endings fails with a misleading error:
#
#   bash: ./scripts/pull-workflows.sh: /usr/bin/env: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# ...because the shebang line ends up as "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r". Pinning eol=lf
# stops git's autocrlf from ever introducing that.
* text=auto eol=lf
